  "body": "I am getting the below error while trying to register new users through the Cient-Server-API on a local (dev) machine:\r\n\r\n`Client error: POST http://localhost:8008/_matrix/client/r0/register?kind=user resulted in a 401 Unauthorized response: {\"errcode\":\"M_MISSING_TOKEN\",\"error\":\"Invalid Authorization header.\"} `\r\n\r\nThe login of the initial user account works fine through the API.\r\n\r\nRegistration specific settings in homeserver.yaml: \r\n-- The homeserver registration is enabled (\"enable_registration: True\").\r\n-- \"registration_shared_secret\" is set, however, not used in this scenario.\r\n-- \"registrations_require_3pid\" is commented / disabled.\r\n\r\nThe following Json is posted: \r\n`{\"kind\":\"user\",\"auth\":{\"type\":\"m.login.dummy\"},\"username\":\"myusername\",\"password\":\"myusername\"}`\r\n\r\n\r\nHow do I have to authorize such a registration request? Obviously a token is missing.\r\n",
